@startuml SD-02-reset-password
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor white
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor black
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor white
skinparam ActorBorderColor black
skinparam BoundaryBackgroundColor white
skinparam BoundaryBorderColor black
skinparam ControlBackgroundColor white
skinparam ControlBorderColor black
skinparam EntityBackgroundColor white
skinparam EntityBorderColor black
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor black
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor black
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor white
skinparam SequenceReferenceBackgroundColor white
skinparam SequenceReferenceBorderColor black
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor white
skinparam NoteBorderColor black
skinparam dpi 150
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam wrapWidth 300
skinparam sequenceParticipantFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceActorFontSize 12
autonumber
title SD-02: Reset Password (UC-02)
' Traces: UC-02; FR-06, FR-66; NFR-09, NFR-11
' Current reset-token policy: DEC-71; member-approved UC-02 review.
' Round-2 detail sources: DEC-61.
' Sources: DEC-17; DEC-55, DEC-56; sequence-diagram-review.md.
' Round-2 source: DEC-58; sequence-diagram-review-round-2.md.
actor User
boundary ":LoginPage" as LP
control ":AuthController" as AC
entity ":Account" as ACC
entity ":AuditLog" as AL
actor "Email Service" as ES

[-> LP : openReset()
activate LP
User -> LP : requestReset(email)
LP -> AC ++ : requestReset(email)
AC -> AC : findAccount(email)
opt account exists and is active
  AC -> ACC ++ : createResetToken()
  ACC --> AC -- : token
  AC -> ES : sendResetLink(email, token)
  ES --> AC : accepted
  AC -> AL : record(User,password reset requested)
end
AC --> LP -- : generic confirmation
LP --> User : If registered, a link was sent
User -> LP : openLink(token)
User -> LP : submitNewPassword(password)
LP -> AC ++ : resetPassword(token, password)
group atomic token validation and password save (NFR-09)
AC -> ACC ++ : validateResetToken(token)
ACC --> AC -- : valid / invalid
alt token valid
  AC -> ACC : setPassword(password)
  AC -> ACC : invalidateResetTokens()
  AC -> AL : record(User, password changed)
  AC --> LP : reset confirmed
else token invalid
  AC --> LP : refuse; request another link
end
end
deactivate AC
LP --> User : reset outcome
deactivate LP
legend bottom
Password is stored only as a salted hash (NFR-11).
Failed saves retain the old password; up to 3 retries, then advise
retry / IT Administrator.
A successful reset invalidates all outstanding reset tokens for
that Account, including earlier reset emails (DEC-71).
Validation occurs inside the atomic save; invalidated tokens cannot
commit another reset. Failed saves retain prior token state.
Token lifetime and password complexity remain open (DEC-61).
endlegend
@enduml
